# The tenth tooling step's breaks.

# Records that do not conflict (item 1): the open items' index written from
# the items, and the records of a step's parts.

[break] outstanding-index-is-not-compared
rule: `rules` fails when the open items' index is not what `cargo xtask outstanding` writes, whatever a merge left in it.
file: xtask/src/rules/layout.rs
in: stale_index
find: (found != expected).then
replace: (false).then
caught-by:
    rules::layout::tests::an_index_that_is_not_what_the_items_give_is_found

[break] outstanding-index-in-file-order
rule: The index lists the items of an area by name, so that it does not depend on the order the files were read in.
file: xtask/src/outstanding.rs
in: index
find: .then_with(|| a.name.cmp(&b.name))
replace:
caught-by:
    outstanding::tests::the_index_lists_every_item_once_by_area_then_name

[break] outstanding-named-areas-before-the-crates
rule: The crates come first in the index, then the named areas in their order.
file: xtask/src/outstanding.rs
in: heading
find: .map_or((0, area), |at| (at + 1, AREAS[at].1))
replace: .map_or((9, area), |at| (at + 1, AREAS[at].1))
caught-by:
    outstanding::tests::the_index_lists_every_item_once_by_area_then_name

[break] outstanding-a-line-twice-is-not-named
rule: A line a merge left twice in the index is named as such.
file: xtask/src/outstanding.rs
in: difference
find: .count() > 1
replace: .count() > 2
caught-by:
    outstanding::tests::a_difference_names_lines_lacking_extra_and_twice
    rules::layout::tests::an_index_that_is_not_what_the_items_give_is_found

[break] outstanding-index-judged-beside-unreadable-items
rule: The index is not judged while an item's file cannot be read; the item's own problem is said first.
